<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiao He</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 193 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xiao He was the chancellor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>. He secured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> archives when the rebels took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianyang">Xianyang</a>, kept the armies supplied from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanzhong">Guanzhong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> during the war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, and as first chancellor of the Han drafted its laws on Qin models.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiao-he.jpg" alt="Xiao He" width="320" height="477" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Xiao_He.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
